# THE PLAYTEST MAP. Not a test fixture -- the tests keep their own segments
# (test_flat, test_ascent) so that tuning this one for feel can never break the
# gate, and the gate can never constrain what this one is allowed to be.
#
# 15 cells (30 m) across. Wide enough for a party to spread out and for a plinko
# field to have lanes, narrow enough that a shove crosses most of it and you can
# always see what your friends are doing.
#
# TWO REAL STEPS, height 0 -> 2 -> 4, so the climb repeats rather than happening
# once. Each step offers all three ascenders side by side, which is the point of
# the map: a group can compare them in one walk.
#
#   x 1-2    GENTLE ramp  -- 1 height unit per cell (~27 deg). Walkable alone.
#   x 7-8    STEEP ramp   -- 2 units per cell (45 deg). Above max_walk_slope, so
#                            no single-player solution: shove or rope.
#   x 12-13  LADDER       -- free, the ordinary case.
#
# Rows 7 and 13 are the cliffs: everything that is not an ascender is a hole, so
# the deck above can ONLY be entered through one of the three.
#
# The walk:
#   z 0-1    flat entry, two pillars to shove around
#   z 2-3    a gap to walk past
#   z 4-5    NO PARAPET on both sides -- the exposed run, with a pillar on it
#   z 6-7    first ascent, to height 2
#   z 8-11   middle deck, two gaps and pillars
#   z 12-13  second ascent, to height 4
#   z 14-15  upper deck, a pillar cluster
#   z 16-17  WATER channel across the middle (geometry only until M7)
#   z 18-21  the run out
#
# READY FOR WHAT IS NOT BUILT YET: water cells are already authored and build as
# a lowered channel, so M7 only adds the flow force. A plinko shooter is the `O`
# glyph and the loader already collects those cells, so M6 only adds the thing
# that stands there. The pillar clusters at z 11 and 15 are deliberately placed
# to be a ricochet field when balls arrive.

name = playtest_bridge
base_height = 0
width = 15
length = 22
tags = foot, playtest, ramp, ladder, water, two_step

